+    WHY (founder, 2026-09-02, 0C.49): 0 of 2,050 archived findings are linked
+    across models -- when two models find one defect the registry mints two
+    unlinked canonicals, so a saturation curve built from source_model is
+    linear by construction and the scaling question ("when does asking another
+    model stop paying?") cannot even be asked of the data.
